class:: FeatureDelta
summary:: Regression derivative of a control feature
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/Slope

description::
For a symmetric radius N, computes sum(n*(x[t+n]-x[t-n])) / (2*sum(n.squared)*frameTime). The window is evaluated causally with N updates of delay. This is the regression delta from the HTK Book, with an explicit seconds scale.

A negative trigger accepts every control block. A nonnegative trigger accepts only positive edges and holds the output between edges; this lets the caller align updates with analysis frames. frameTime must match that regular update spacing. Irregular triggers do not create a nonuniform regression. Nonfinite input is replaced by zero. The first output appears after 2*radius+1 accepted values. Cost is O(radius) per accepted update and memory is fixed. Source: link::https://labrosa.ee.columbia.edu/doc/HTKBook21/node56.html::. Vanilla Slope is a one-step difference; regression uses a symmetric span of observations.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: in
Control-rate or scalar feature, with multichannel expansion for feature arrays.

argument:: radius
Literal symmetric regression radius from 1 through 32; total support is 2*radius+1 per regression pass.

argument:: trigger
Negative: update every control block. Otherwise update on positive edges.

argument:: frameTime
Seconds between accepted values. Zero uses the server control period; supply the actual period when triggering sparsely.

returns::
Derivative in input units per second.

examples::
FeatureDelta calculates the causal regression first derivative of any control-rate feature stream. In this example, the velocity of spectral centroid changes is tracked on a drum groove: rapid upward spectral surges trigger a resonant micro-glitch stutter delay, accentuating transient attacks. An interactive code::MIR2GUI.scope:: plots the real-time feature derivative.
code::
(
Routine({
    var path = MIR2GUI.soundPath("drums.wav");
    ~mir2Buffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~mir2Bus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1);
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, hop: 0.5);
        var centroid = SpecCentroid2.kr(chain, fftSize: 1024);
        var delta = FeatureDelta.kr(centroid, radius: 2, trigger: -1, frameTime: 0.01);
        var surge = (delta > 2000);
        var glitchDelay = CombN.ar(source * surge.lag(0.005), 0.2, 0.04, 0.3);
        var sound = (source * 0.25) + (glitchDelay * 0.35);

        if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { Out.kr(~mir2Bus, delta) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2) ! 2
    }.play;

    ~mir2GUI = MIR2GUI.scope("Spectral Centroid Delta", ~mir2Bus, -4000.0, 4000.0, "Hz/s");
}).play(AppClock);
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
if(~mir2GUI.notNil) { ~mir2GUI.close };
if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { ~mir2Bus.free };
if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) { ~mir2Buffer.free };
)
::

